50:        <h1>CEO Agents</h1>
70:        <details>
88:      <section class="chapter-section" id="orientation">
90:        <h2 class="section-title">Begin with the promotion</h2>
97:        <aside class="callout callout--tactic">
102:        <h3>What you are training</h3>
110:        <h3>The source discipline for this chapter</h3>
118:        <h3>How to study a dense chapter</h3>
124:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="innovations">
126:        <h2 class="section-title">Stack three unlocks, not one trick</h2>
131:          <h3>A brilliant prompt in a machine that cannot sustain it</h3>
138:          <h3>Capacity · control · compounding</h3>
140:            <article class="innovation-card" data-n="1"><p class="eyebrow">Capacity</p><h3>Useful long context</h3><p>Hold the brief, context files, system prompt, debate, and accumulated expertise without a sharp retrieval cliff.</p></article>
141:            <article class="innovation-card" data-n="2"><p class="eyebrow">Control</p><h3>Custom agent harness</h3><p>Register meeting tools, replace the coding persona, spawn persistent board sessions, lock input, render the TUI, and enforce constraints.</p></article>
142:            <article class="innovation-card" data-n="3"><p class="eyebrow">Compounding</p><h3>Domain expertise</h3><p>Give each seat a persistent, updatable scratch pad focused on the patterns and tensions that matter to its role.</p></article>
149:          <h3>The context claim is about retrieval, not the advertised number</h3>
151:          <figure class="frame-card">
156:          <figure class="frame-card">
164:          <h3>True long context · customizable harness · expertise</h3>
165:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
175:          <h3>Follow the acquisition meeting through the stack</h3>
184:          <h3>Assign each behavior to its enabling layer</h3>
198:          <h3>Failure: calling accumulated text “learning”</h3>
205:          <h3>Recheck capacity claims; keep the architecture</h3>
206:          <aside class="current-practice">
214:          <h3>Recover the stack from memory</h3>
215:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for the three innovations">
216:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Why is long context the enabling innovation?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The system needs to retain a whole brief, supporting context, a multi-round debate, persistent session state, and growing expertise. The other innovations create the information load.</p></details></div>
217:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. How is expertise different from a raw memory dump?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Expertise is persistent memory and patterns scoped to a specific role and problem domain, with an explicit use condition and update behavior.</p></details></div>
218:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. What must another harness expose to carry this pattern?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>At minimum, control over the system prompt, custom tool registration, subprocess or subagent execution, persistent member sessions, context loading, and enough lifecycle hooks to enforce the meeting workflow.</p></details></div>
225:            <h3>Explain why “a bigger model” is incomplete</h3>
231:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="constraints">
233:        <h2 class="section-title">Bound the meeting like it matters</h2>
238:          <h3>The board that can always think one more thought</h3>
245:          <h3>Two gauges, four boundaries</h3>
255:          <h3>The constraints stay visible from the first screen</h3>
257:          <figure class="frame-card">
262:          <figure class="frame-card">
267:          <figure class="frame-card">
275:          <h3>Make “enough” and “too much” executable</h3>
276:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
285:          <h3>A $5 demonstration is not a $5 philosophy</h3>
293:          <h3>Set three envelopes before touching the config</h3>
305:          <h3>Failure: treating the ceiling as a timer interrupt</h3>
312:          <h3>Constraint design travels across harnesses</h3>
313:          <aside class="current-practice">
321:          <h3>Retrieve the state machine</h3>
322:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for meeting constraints">
323:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. What does the 80% threshold do?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>It flags that a time or budget maximum is approaching so the CEO should begin wrapping rather than opening broad new lines of debate.</p></details></div>
324:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. What changes when a maximum is hit?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Further <code>converse</code> calls are blocked and the CEO is instructed to call <code>end_deliberation</code>, collect final statements, and write the memo.</p></details></div>
325:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Why have a minimum at all?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>A floor protects the decision from premature synthesis. In the v1 implementation, minimum time is the programmatically enforced early-close guard; the minimum-budget claim needs technical scrutiny later in the chapter.</p></details></div>
332:            <h3>Explain floors and ceilings to a finance partner</h3>
338:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="prompts">
340:        <h2 class="section-title">Template the question before scaling the answer</h2>
345:          <h3>“What should I do?” is not a strategic brief</h3>
352:          <h3>Separate fact, consequence, boundary, and question</h3>
364:          <h3>One readable file defines the meeting’s outer shape</h3>
366:          <figure class="frame-card">
375:          <h3>Template your engineering</h3>
376:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
385:          <h3>From one sentence to an inspectable decision</h3>
393:          <h3>Write the failure before the success</h3>
405:          <h3>Failure: a valid shell with empty substance</h3>
412:          <h3>Prefer schemas you can test</h3>
413:          <aside class="current-practice">
421:          <h3>Rebuild the brief from a blank page</h3>
422:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for brief validation">
423:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Name the four required headings in order.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Situation, Stakes, Constraints, and Key Question.</p></details></div>
424:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. What happens to sibling Markdown files?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Every <code>.md</code> file in the brief directory other than <code>brief.md</code> is treated as context and passed to each board member on first contact.</p></details></div>
425:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. What does passing validation not prove?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>It does not prove the facts are specific, accurate, sufficient, unbiased, or sourced. The v1 check establishes that required section strings are present.</p></details></div>
432:            <h3>Teach prompt engineering without mentioning clever wording</h3>
438:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="decision">
440:        <h2 class="section-title">Promote agents from production to judgment</h2>
445:          <h3>A fast team building the wrong thing</h3>
452:          <h3>Brief → deliberation → memo</h3>
465:          <h3>The acquisition question arrives as a real artifact</h3>
467:          <figure class="frame-card">
472:          <figure class="frame-card">
480:          <h3>Agentic engineering</h3>
481:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
491:          <h3>Trace one fact from input to decision</h3>
498:          <h3>Turn one worry into a three-node system</h3>
510:          <h3>Failure: an executive-flavored chat</h3>
517:          <h3>The pattern is more durable than the model roster</h3>
518:          <aside class="current-practice">
526:          <h3>Answer before opening</h3>
527:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for decisions not code">
528:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. State the whole system in three nodes.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Brief → deliberation → memo: structured uncertainty enters, an adversarial workflow tests it, and a decision artifact leaves.</p></details></div>
529:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. Why is a saved memo better than a persuasive chat answer?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The memo has a stable schema that preserves ranked recommendations, individual stances, dissent, trade-offs, risks, and next actions for later inspection.</p></details></div>
530:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Why can different vote totals be acceptable?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The agents are nondeterministic. The system should preserve the reasoning and recurring dissent rather than claim an identical vote is guaranteed on every run.</p></details></div>
537:            <h3>Explain the promotion in ninety seconds</h3>
543:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="board">
545:        <h2 class="section-title">Design the board to disagree</h2>
550:          <h3>The expensive echo chamber</h3>
557:          <h3>Eight objective functions around one decision</h3>
573:          <h3>The CEO does not contain the board; it orchestrates it</h3>
575:          <figure class="frame-card">
580:          <figure class="frame-card">
588:          <h3>Multi-agent adversarial pattern</h3>
589:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
599:          <h3>From seven votes to one better condition</h3>
607:          <h3>Make two agents unable to give the same answer</h3>
619:          <h3>Failure: persona theater</h3>
626:          <h3>Model diversity can sharpen role diversity</h3>
627:          <aside class="current-practice">
635:          <h3>Retrieve the board, not just the names</h3>
636:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for adversarial boards">
637:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Why is disagreement a feature rather than a coordination failure?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Specialists are designed to expose different blind spots. Their conflict makes trade-offs visible and can improve the majority recommendation with conditions or tests.</p></details></div>
638:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. Name two natural tension pairs and the trade-off each embodies.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Revenue versus Compounder pits near-term cash against durable trust. Customer Oracle versus Moonshot pits immediate adoption reality against asymmetric long-term upside. Product versus Technical pits strategic wedge selection against production durability.</p></details></div>
639:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. What makes a role more than a costume?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>An explicit objective function, time horizon, risk tolerance, default stance, evidence standard, red lines, reasoning patterns, and tension partners change how the agent decides.</p></details></div>
646:            <h3>Defend the dissenter</h3>
652:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="observability">
654:        <h2 class="section-title">Trust the code and keep the evidence</h2>
659:          <h3>The beautiful memo with no inspectable path</h3>
666:          <h3>Primary agent → custom tool → persistent subprocesses → log</h3>
677:          <h3>Logs turn a performance into a system you can audit</h3>
679:          <figure class="frame-card">
688:          <h3>Measure the deliberation you want to improve</h3>
689:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
698:          <h3>Three checks a careful operator should make</h3>
713:          <h3>Prove one claim at three levels</h3>
725:          <h3>Failure: overclaiming from log order</h3>
732:          <h3>Recheck the shipping implementation</h3>
733:          <aside class="current-practice">
741:          <h3>Separate promise, implementation, and evidence</h3>
742:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for observability and runtime truth">
743:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. How is the CEO run differently from a board member?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The CEO is the primary Pi agent with a system prompt injected by the extension. Board members run as separate <code>pi</code> subprocesses with their own prompts, models, and persistent session files.</p></details></div>
744:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. State the safest round-sharing model.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Selected members launch concurrently within a round, so ordered same-round cross-pollination is not guaranteed. Across rounds, members can reliably reread the shared conversation log.</p></details></div>
745:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. Name the three v1 gaps audited here.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Converse is concurrent rather than sequentially fed; Contrarian is not serialized last; and the early-close guard enforces minimum time but not minimum budget.</p></details></div>
746:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">4. Which two files form the minimum audit trail?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p><code>conversation.jsonl</code> for meeting exchanges and <code>tool-use.jsonl</code> for recorded tool activity. The memo, sessions, expertise diffs, and generated assets add context.</p></details></div>
753:            <h3>Narrate a round like an implementer</h3>
759:      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="specialize">
761:        <h2 class="section-title">Specialize the whole system</h2>
766:          <h3>The average agent with a grand title</h3>
773:          <h3>Change more than context</h3>
785:          <h3>The memo becomes a decision package</h3>
787:          <figure class="frame-card">
796:          <h3>Micro-applications, agentically</h3>
797:          <aside class="callout callout--term">
806:          <h3>Five changes, five ownership layers</h3>
820:          <h3>Diagnose a proposed “expert agent”</h3>
832:          <h3>Failure: adding capability without narrowing purpose</h3>
839:          <h3>Portable primitives outlast product churn</h3>
840:          <aside class="current-practice">
848:          <h3>Retrieve the specialization levers</h3>
849:          <section class="retrieval-quiz" aria-label="Retrieval questions for specialization">
850:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">1. Name the core four.</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>Context, model, prompt, and tools.</p></details></div>
851:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">2. Why is richer context alone not enough?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>The model, objective function, action surface, session behavior, and completion contract can still remain generic. Specialization changes multiple dimensions.</p></details></div>
852:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">3. What inputs does the one-shot interface accept?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p><code>/ceo-begin</code> starts a meeting, <code>stop</code> hard-stops it, and <code>wrap</code> requests early synthesis. Other typed input is intercepted.</p></details></div>
853:            <div class="retrieval-quiz__item"><p class="retrieval-quiz__q">4. Why declare a skill with “use when”?</p><details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>It keeps a reusable capability available without forcing it into every turn. The agent can read and run the skill when the decision artifact needs it.</p></details></div>
860:            <h3>Explain why this is not “eight chatbots”</h3>
--- SHARED TOKENS ---
/* ============================================================
   IndyDevDan Expert Book — design tokens (light teaching theme)
   Single source of truth. Chapters must consume these variables;
   no ad-hoc colors or type sizes in chapter HTML.
   Skeleton only — extend via new tokens, don't fork values inline.
   ============================================================ */

:root {
  /* ---------- color: surfaces (warm cream, no heavy dark mode) ---------- */
  --bg:          #FAF6EF;   /* page — warm off-white cream */
  --bg-card:     #FFFFFF;   /* raised cards, code frames */
  --bg-inset:    #F1EAE0;   /* wells, quiz bodies, table stripes */
  --bg-code:     #F6F1E8;   /* code blocks (slightly warmer than card) */
  --border:      #E2D9CA;   /* hairline card borders */
  --border-soft: #EDE6D9;   /* subtle dividers */

  /* ---------- color: ink ---------- */
  --ink:         #211E19;   /* primary text — warm near-black */
  --ink-soft:    #4C463C;   /* secondary text, captions */
  --ink-mute:    #85796A;   /* metadata, labels, timestamps */

  /* ---------- color: the one accent ---------- */
  --accent:       #B4530A;  /* tactical clay-orange — links, highlights, tactic marks */
  --accent-ink:   #8A3F06;  /* accent on cream at small sizes (AA) */
  --accent-wash:  #F7E7D8;  /* accent tint for callout fills / selection */

  /* functional colors (quiz feedback + danger callouts only — not brand) */
  --ok:          #3D7A4E;
  --ok-wash:     #E4EFE6;
  --warn:        #A33D2E;
  --warn-wash:   #F6E4E0;

  /* chapter illustration + terminal surfaces */
  --ink-inverse:     #FFFFFF;
  --teach-wash:      #ECE3F4;
  --terminal-border: #D3C9BA;
  --terminal-bg:     #27231F;
  --terminal-ink:    #F5EFE7;
  --terminal-bar:    #39332D;
  --terminal-dot:    #D7C6AE;

  /* ---------- type ---------- */
  /* Display webfont is OPTIONAL. If Fraunces is self-hosted later, add the
     @font-face in base.css; these stacks degrade cleanly without it. */
  --font-display: "Fraunces", "Iowan Old Style", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
  --font-body:    -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-mono:    ui-monospace, "SF Mono", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;

  /* type scale (1.25 ratio on 1rem=16px base; print-friendly) */
  --text-xs:   0.75rem;    /* 12 — fine print, frame credits */
  --text-sm:   0.875rem;   /* 14 — captions, labels, code */
  --text-base: 1.0625rem;  /* 17 — body prose */
  --text-md:   1.25rem;    /* 20 — lead paragraphs, h4 */
  --text-lg:   1.5625rem;  /* 25 — h3 */
  --text-xl:   1.9375rem;  /* 31 — h2 */
  --text-2xl:  2.4375rem;  /* 39 — h1 / chapter titles */
  --text-3xl:  3.0625rem;  /* 49 — volume covers only */
  --text-diagram-sm: 1rem;
  --text-diagram-md: 1.125rem;
  --text-diagram-lg: 1.25rem;
  --text-diagram-xl: 1.6875rem;
  --text-diagram-2xl: 1.9375rem;
  --text-print: 10.5pt;

  --leading-tight: 1.15;   /* display headings */
  --leading-snug:  1.35;   /* h3/h4, quiz options */
  --leading-body:  1.65;   /* prose */

  --measure: 66ch;         /* max prose line length */

  /* ---------- spacing (4px base) ---------- */
  --space-1:  0.25rem;
  --space-2:  0.5rem;
  --space-3:  0.75rem;
  --space-4:  1rem;
  --space-5:  1.5rem;
  --space-6:  2rem;
  --space-8:  3rem;
  --space-10: 4rem;
  --space-12: 6rem;

  /* ---------- shape & elevation ---------- */
  --radius-sm: 6px;        /* inline chips, quiz options */
  --radius-md: 10px;       /* callouts, lab boxes */
  --radius-lg: 16px;       /* frame cards, diagrams */
  --shadow-card: 0 1px 2px rgba(33, 30, 25, 0.06), 0 4px 16px rgba(33, 30, 25, 0.05);

  /* ---------- misc ---------- */
  --hairline: 1px solid var(--border);
  --content-max: 46rem;    /* chapter column */
  --wide-max: 62rem;       /* diagrams / frame grids may break out to this */
}
--- BASE ---
/* ============================================================
   IndyDevDan Expert Book — base: reset + prose defaults
   Requires tokens.css loaded first.
   ============================================================ */

*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

* { margin: 0; }

html {
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}

body {
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: var(--text-base);
  line-height: var(--leading-body);
  text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}

img, svg, video { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; }

::selection { background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--ink); }

:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
  outline-offset: 2px;
  border-radius: 2px;
}

/* ---------- prose ---------- */

.prose {
  max-width: var(--content-max);
  margin-inline: auto;
  padding-inline: var(--space-4);
}

.prose > * + * { margin-top: var(--space-4); }

h1, h2, h3 {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-wrap: balance;
}

h1 { font-size: var(--text-2xl); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl);  margin-top: var(--space-8); }
h3 { font-size: var(--text-lg);  margin-top: var(--space-6); line-height: var(--leading-snug); }
h4 { font-size: var(--text-md);  margin-top: var(--space-5); line-height: var(--leading-snug); font-weight: 650; }

p, li { max-width: var(--measure); }

ul, ol { padding-left: 1.4em; }
li + li { margin-top: var(--space-2); }

a {
  color: var(--accent-ink);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
  text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
}
a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }

strong { font-weight: 650; }

blockquote {
  border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  color: var(--ink-soft);
  font-style: italic;
}
blockquote cite { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); font-style: normal; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--ink-mute); }

hr { border: 0; border-top: var(--hairline); margin-block: var(--space-8); }

/* ---------- code ---------- */

code, kbd, samp, pre {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 0.9em;
}

code {
  background: var(--bg-code);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
}

pre {
  background: var(--bg-code);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--space-4);
  overflow-x: auto;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
pre code { background: none; border: 0; padding: 0; font-size: var(--text-sm); }

/* ---------- tables ---------- */

table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  width: 100%;
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
}
th, td {
  text-align: left;
  padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
  border-bottom: var(--hairline);
  vertical-align: top;
}
th { font-weight: 650; color: var(--ink-soft); }
tbody tr:nth-child(even) { background: var(--bg-inset); }

/* ---------- small print ---------- */

figcaption, .fine { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--ink-mute); }
--- COMPONENTS ---
/* ============================================================
   IndyDevDan Expert Book — component stubs
   Contracts for the chapter builder. Each block documents its
   expected markup. Visual detail intentionally minimal — extend
   here, never inline in chapters.
   Requires tokens.css + base.css.
   ============================================================ */

/* ---------- callout ------------------------------------------------
   <aside class="callout callout--tactic|--term|--warning|--why">
     <p class="callout__label">Tactic #1</p>
     <p>…</p>
   </aside>
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.callout {
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
}
.callout__label {
  font-size: var(--text-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent-ink);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}
.callout--tactic  { background: var(--accent-wash); }
.callout--term    { border-left-color: var(--ink-soft); }   /* "Dan's term" definitions */
.callout--term .callout__label { color: var(--ink-soft); }
.callout--warning { border-left-color: var(--warn); background: var(--warn-wash); }
.callout--warning .callout__label { color: var(--warn); }
.callout--why     { border-left-color: var(--ok); }         /* "why this matters" asides */
.callout--why .callout__label { color: var(--ok); }

/* ---------- diagram -------------------------------------------------
   <figure class="diagram">
     <div class="diagram__canvas"> …inline SVG or structured HTML… </div>
     <figcaption>…</figcaption>
   </figure>
   Used when a redrawn diagram beats a video frame (frame_plan.diagram_instead).
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.diagram {
  max-width: var(--wide-max);
  margin-inline: auto;
}
.diagram__canvas {
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  padding: var(--space-6);
}
.diagram figcaption { margin-top: var(--space-2); text-align: center; }

/* ---------- frame-card ----------------------------------------------
   <figure class="frame-card">
     <img src="../media/frames/tac-1/t0845-core-four.jpg" alt="…">
     <figcaption><span class="frame-card__t">14:05</span> …why this frame matters…</figcaption>
   </figure>
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.frame-card {
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  max-width: var(--wide-max);
  margin-inline: auto;
}
.frame-card img { width: 100%; }
.frame-card figcaption { padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); }
.frame-card__t {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: var(--text-xs);
  color: var(--accent-ink);
  background: var(--accent-wash);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: 0.1em 0.5em;
  margin-right: var(--space-2);
}

/* ---------- lab-box --------------------------------------------------
   <section class="lab-box">
     <h3 class="lab-box__title">Lab 1.1 — Reproduce Dan</h3>
     <ol class="lab-box__steps">…</ol>
     <div class="lab-box__pass"><h4>Pass criteria</h4><ul>…</ul></div>
   </section>
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.lab-box {
  background: var(--bg-inset);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  padding: var(--space-5);
}
.lab-box__title { margin-top: 0; }
.lab-box__pass {
  margin-top: var(--space-4);
  background: var(--bg-card);
  border-left: 4px solid var(--ok);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
}

/* ---------- retrieval-quiz -------------------------------------------
   <section class="retrieval-quiz">
     <div class="retrieval-quiz__item">
       <p class="retrieval-quiz__q">Q. …</p>
       <details class="retrieval-quiz__a"><summary>Reveal answer</summary><p>…</p></details>
     </div>
   </section>
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.retrieval-quiz {
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-card);
  padding: var(--space-5);
}
.retrieval-quiz__item + .retrieval-quiz__item {
  margin-top: var(--space-4);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
  padding-top: var(--space-4);
}
.retrieval-quiz__q { font-weight: 650; }
.retrieval-quiz__a summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  color: var(--accent-ink);
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
  margin-top: var(--space-2);
}
.retrieval-quiz__a[open] summary { color: var(--ink-mute); }
.retrieval-quiz__a p {
  margin-top: var(--space-2);
  background: var(--ok-wash);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  padding: var(--space-3);
}

/* ---------- current-practice ------------------------------------------
   "What changed since the course" overlay blocks.
   <aside class="current-practice">
     <p class="current-practice__label">Current practice · 2026</p>
     <p>…gap + what to do today…</p>
     <p class="current-practice__source">Overlay: <a href="…">RAW Agentic Coding: ZERO to Agent SKILL</a></p>
   </aside>
-------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.current-practice {
  border: 1px dashed var(--accent);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-card);
  padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
}
.current-practice__label {
  font-size: var(--text-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--accent-ink);
  margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
}
.current-practice__source { font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--ink-mute); margin-top: var(--space-3); }


/* Fan-out: large readable teaching frames */
.frame-card,
.figure-frame,
figure.teaching-frame {
  margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  max-width: min(100%, 72rem);
}
.frame-card img,
.figure-frame img,
figure.teaching-frame img,
.chapter-main img.frame,
.chapter-main .frame-card img {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: min(100%, 1100px);
  height: auto;
  display: block;
  margin-inline: auto;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
  image-rendering: -webkit-optimize-contrast;
  background: #fff;
}
.frame-card figcaption,
figure.teaching-frame figcaption {
  margin-top: 0.65rem;
  font-size: 0.95rem;
  line-height: 1.45;
  color: var(--ink-muted, #475569);
  max-width: 70ch;
  margin-inline: auto;
}
.generated-plate img {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: min(100%, 1000px);
  height: auto;
  display: block;
  margin: 1rem auto;
  border-radius: 14px;
}

