vol-3-ma/16-lead-agents.html:411:            <p><strong>Domain locking:</strong> explicit per-agent, per-path permissions that control reading, creating/updating, and deleting, enforced by the runtime rather than trusted to the prompt alone.</p>
vol-3-ma/16-lead-agents.html:425:          <p>Bash is harder because a shell string can hide writes. The enforcer uses heuristics to detect write and delete patterns rather than assuming that <code>bash</code> is harmless. This does not turn shell parsing into a perfect sandbox; it does make the course’s domain contract structural across the ordinary file tools and common shell mutations.</p>
